# Rust build output — big, regenerable, never committed.
# NOTE the leading-slash trap: `/target` matches ONLY the repo root. A nested
# crate (analysis/census) built in place slipped 3,894 files and 889 MB past it
# in commit 0d9420d. The unanchored form below matches at any depth.
target/

# Local environment: RPC keys, DATABASE_URL. Never commit these.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Run exports: reproducible from Postgres + the pinned commit, never committed.
/data

# Working notes stay private; PUBLISHED reports are part of the record.
#
# The split is between what a reader can check and what is internal project
# state. docs/reports/ holds census reports that findings are cited from —
# those are the product. Handoffs, launch checklists and publication runbooks
# are scaffolding: they carry no claim anyone can verify, and a reader who
# stumbles into a half-finished checklist learns nothing true about the census.
#
# DRAFT-* reports are excluded for a sharper reason: one of them opens with
# "NO FIGURES until the rerun completes" and is entirely placeholders. A
# skeleton published beside real reports is worse than absent.
/docs/*
!/docs/reports/
/docs/reports/DRAFT-*
